{"seq":26,"trial_id":"v03-pilot-2026-10/hermes-haiku-gbrain-told-scoped-mu-v03-dev/sy-03-marrow-fieldworks-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-10-29T16:34:52.955Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-16T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"f9724500ff7cc8036cc73fbf994902e25d91aba62350bce41b29fe874438da84","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03PIL0001","text":"Pree, here are the Marrow Fieldworks (MFW) ticket numbers I can see across #central-random, #central-team, Moss's notes and the Central weekly and handoff notes. Several numbers conflict between sources, and I've flagged those.\n\nMFW tickets:\n- PD-5302: #central-random, Hollis, Oct 14. Follow-up from this week. No action taken. I only acknowledged it there; it isn't logged anywhere else.\n- #8841: #central-random, Tobias, Oct 13. He flagged West yard Door 2 double-booking at the kiosk on it. Conflict: the Feb 10, 2025 Central weekly uses #8841 for a Tansley Parcel printer jam.\n- PD-88412: Central weekly Jul 13, 2026. Salina flatbeds not auto-assigning to Doors 14 and 15. Conflict: #88412 in #central-team (Jul 2025) is Tansleigh Packaging, and Moss's Marrow Agrisupply cheat sheet cites PD-88412 for a Daily Yard Dwell complaint.\n- #4409 and #4412: Moss's Jan 2, 2026 handoff digest. Two open tickets on your dealer account before the handoff (Gatehouse Check-In timeout at Salina North; SMS prompt glitch on overflow lots).\n- MFW-218: CRM note, Apr 23, 2026 (renewal). Door 4/6 reassignment at the west receiving entrance; dispatch screenshots and arrival sheet go on the ticket.\n- SUP-4630: dealer portal SSO loop, Dec 2, 2025 (team-central ticket note).\n- ZD-44918: Apr 8, 2025 MSA signing call notes. Onboarding ticket linked to a sandbox trial. Not confirmed as still open.\n- #4419: Hollis's Dec 15, 2025 email says Salina yard gate 3 barcode scanner (MFW). Moss's notes tie #4419 to Quarrendon Freight Lines. Conflict; not resolved.\n\nNot clearly MFW: PD-4821 (#central-team, Jun 9, 2026) is in the Marrow Agrisupply store rollout thread, so it's probably MAS.\n\nLeft out as other accounts: #4418 and FR-882 and SUP-88201 and PD-88309 (Marrow Agrisupply), PD-88490 (Tansleigh), PD-4492 (Quarrendon), INC-44912 and CENTRAL-184 (Tansley), HR-409 (internal)."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03PIL0001","ts":"1792159200.000127"}}
